Multi-material tool ordering: fix OOB indexing family + never-initialized
filament option keys (the WASM painted-slice crash class).

Slicing any model whose regions use a filament other than #1 crashed the
WASM build ("memory access out of bounds") or silently truncated the
print. Four related defects, one root theme: per-filament vectors and the
code that indexes them disagree about the filament count.

1. PrintConfigDef's constructor calls init_extruder_option_keys() but
   never init_filament_option_keys(), so m_filament_option_keys is empty
   and DynamicPrintConfig::set_num_filaments() is a silent no-op — the
   per-filament vectors (filament_diameter, filament_colour, ...) can
   never be programmatically sized. Call it.

2. calc_filament_change_info_by_toolorder() indexes filament_map and the
   flush matrix with layer-sequence filament ids without bounds checks.
   A config whose filament_colour is shorter than the filaments actually
   used (e.g. a comma-joined colour list — ConfigOptionStrings splits on
   ';') read wild memory: OOB trap on wasm32, silent UB on native arm64.
   Guard and log instead.

3. cal_most_used_extruder() indexes config.filament_map.values[filament]
   unguarded (the option defaults to {1} and nothing resizes it), then
   uses the garbage result to WRITE extruder_count[garbage]++ — heap
   corruption that surfaced as an abort in emscripten_builtin_free.
   Same for GCodeProcessor::process_filament_change() on the gcode
   post-processing side. Guard both.

4. ToolOrdering sized its filament universe from filament_colour alone
   (get_recommended_filament_maps + reorder_extruders_for_minimum_flush
   _volume) while PrintApply sizes num_extruders from filament_diameter.
   When the two disagree, filaments past filament_colour.size() land in
   no reorder group and their per-layer sequences come back EMPTY —
   m_layer_tools[i].extruders is overwritten with nothing and those
   layers vanish from the G-code (a two-colour print truncated at the
   colour boundary, no error). Size from max(colour, diameter), keep the
   collected extruders when the DP returns an empty layer, and pad the
   recommended-maps flush matrix rather than slicing past its end.

Found via wasm/test_slice_painted.mjs (two stacked cubes on filaments
1+2). Verified: painted slice completes with correct tool changes with
and without a prime tower; single-material slicing unchanged.

Retire-if: upstream initializes filament option keys in the ctor and
bounds-guards its multi-material tool-ordering paths.

